✅ 2. Project Explanation (Fake or Real - Payment Resilience Project)
“In my most recent project, I worked on a Payment Resilience System for a financial services application.
The goal was to ensure high availability and robustness of our payment processing APIs.

We used Spring Boot to build microservices that interact with third-party payment gateways.
To handle failures and ensure resilience, we integrated Resilience4j and implemented:

Retry: Automatically retry failed API calls up to 3 times.
Timeout: Fail requests if no response is received within 3 seconds.
Circuit Breaker: If a gateway fails consistently, we stop sending requests temporarily to allow recovery.
Fallbacks: Provided backup payment options for users.

We also simulated downstream failures and logged them using Splunk for observability.
Nginx acted as our API gateway, and we used Jenkins pipelines for deployment.

This project helped reduce payment failures by 40% and significantly improved user trust in the platform.”